<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bloemfontein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bloemfontein is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, capital of the Free State province and the country's judicial capital. Founded in 1846 by Major Henry Warden as a British post, it became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> and from 1854 of the Orange Free State. It was occupied by the British in 1900, and since 1910 it has been the seat of the country's highest court of appeal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bloemfontein.jpg" alt="Bloemfontein" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: South African Tourism from South Africa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bloemfontein,_Free_State,_South_Africa_(20349855518).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
